   "since": "2026-09-01",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "Oklahoma City National Memorial honors the victims, survivors, rescuers, and all who were changed forever on April 19, 1995. Legislation establishing the Oklahoma City National Memorial (P.L. 105-58) was signed into law by President Clinton in October, 1997. The Oklahoma City National Memorial Trust was organized to create a permanent memorial on the site of the bombing in Oklahoma City to honor those who died, those who survived and those changed forever on April 19, 1995. The Memorial is comprised of three distinct components. [http://www.nps.gov/archive/okci/home.htm]",
